# GrantAI — Grant Intelligence Operating System

**Status:** Draft — founder review required
**Parent framework:** Bridges AI Enterprises Operating System (BAEOS)
**Module type:** Enterprise Module (BAEOS Vol 12 — Platform Capability Module)

## What This Is

GrantAI is a Grant Intelligence Operating System — not a single chatbot, but a
coordinated system of specialized AI agents, knowledge bases, and workflows
that finds, evaluates, drafts, tracks, and learns from grant funding
opportunities on behalf of Bridges AI Enterprises and its client businesses.

It is built as a BAEOS enterprise module: structured Markdown documents meant
to live in a dedicated `docs/` folder in this repo, with a lean `AGENTS.md`
router at the project root (matching the pattern used across the rest of the
BAE portfolio).

## Core Capability

At full build-out, GrantAI:

- Searches thousands of grant opportunities across federal, state, corporate,
  and foundation sources
- Continuously monitors approved sources for new funding as it's posted
- Scores each opportunity against a business's eligibility and fit
- Recommends the highest-value grants to pursue
- Drafts complete grant applications, including budgets
- Tracks deadlines and application status end-to-end
- Learns from the outcomes of previous submissions
- Generates reports and dashboards for founder review
- Coordinates multiple specialized agents (Finder, Writer, Reviewer,
  Researcher, Compliance, Executive Advisor, Hunter) under one governance
  model

## Autonomous Grant Hunter (Flagship Enhancement)

The **Grant Hunter** is what moves GrantAI from "writing assistant" to
"virtual grant department." It runs on a schedule (not on-demand), and:

1. Sweeps only pre-approved funding sources (see `FundingOrganizations.md`)
2. Diffs new/changed listings against the existing `KnowledgeBase`
3. Runs new opportunities through the `EligibilityEngine` and
   `ScoringSystem`
4. Auto-updates the knowledge base with anything that clears the fit
   threshold
5. Prepares a **draft** application package for anything above the
   high-value threshold — draft only, never submitted, never sent, without
   founder approval (Tier 4 decision — see `GOVERNANCE.md`)
6. Produces a digest report of what it found, what it drafted, and what it
   skipped and why

See `GrantHunter-Agent.md` (Phase 2) for the full spec.

